{
  "name": "Menhirkin Heritage: Metamorphic",
  "type": "feat",
  "img": "art/bbttcc/GOTTGAIT/BBTTCC%20Button%20Icons/bbttcc_icons_wyrdlens_adept_23.png",
  "system": {
    "category": "technique",
    "source": "Bad Eden Heritages v1.1 (RFI-native rules)",
    "tags": [],
    "description": {
      "value": "<div data-ft-phase5-vocab-scrub=\"v1\" style=\"display:none\"></div><p><strong>Bad Eden Heritage (v1.1, RFI-native).</strong> Menhirkin heritage: Metamorphic.</p><p><em>“What you are now is not what you were. The pressure was the point.”</em></p><p><strong>Menhirkin (Metamorphic).</strong> You are land that was buried, squeezed, heated, and came back up harder and more interesting. Every Metamorphic has a before-self — a softer version of themselves that got pressed into something else. You remember being that. You are not going back.</p><h3>Traits</h3><ul><li><p><strong>Creature Type.</strong> Humanoid (Menhirkin).</p></li><li><p><strong>Size.</strong> Medium.</p></li><li><p><strong>Movement.</strong> 6 squares walking.</p></li><li><p><strong>Lineage Lean.</strong> Menhirkin does not grant fixed attribute bonuses; your background handles increases. Your heritage leans toward <strong>Body</strong> in fiction and through Tier powers.</p></li></ul><h3>Menhirkin Core: The Land Stood Up</h3><p><em>Shared across all Menhirkin heritages. Granted at character creation via the base ancestry item.</em></p><ul><li><p><strong>Stone Soul.</strong> You count as Large for carry, shove, and grapple despite your Medium frame. You reroll the lowest die on checks to resist being forcibly moved.</p></li><li><p><strong>Hex Recognition.</strong> Once per scene, while you are on a natural surface you are directly touching, you may whisper a single question about the place. The GM answers with one true thing the land knows.</p></li><li><p><strong>Slow to Wear.</strong> You reroll the lowest die on Body checks against Stress, long-duration physical wear, forced marches, climate exposure, and sustained labor. You do not tire the way softer things tire.</p></li><li><p><strong>Heavy Presence.</strong> Your weight and settledness are perceptible. Creatures within 2 squares of you know you are there even if they cannot see you; you roll 3d10 keep lowest 2 on Intrigue (Stealth) checks unless you are on or in stone.</p></li></ul><h3>Metamorphic Traits</h3><ul><li><p><strong>Pressure Remade.</strong> At the end of each Soma Break, the day chooses what you are until your next Soma Break. Roll a d4 or pick (GM discretion): (1) +1 Guard, (2) resistance to kinetic damage, (3) +1 rank on one skill of your choice, (4) reroll-lowest on Body checks to resist being knocked prone or grappled. You announce the result; you do not pre-pick.</p></li><li><p><strong>Unbreakable Core.</strong> You reroll the lowest die on defense checks against petrification, forced transmutation, and forced shape-change. You have been turned into something else once already; nobody does it twice without your say-so.</p></li></ul><h3>Strategic Hooks (Foundry / Bad Eden)</h3><ul><li><p><strong>OP Edge.</strong> Your faction gains <strong>+2 Non-Lethal OP</strong> and <strong>+1 Intrigue OP</strong> at campaign start.</p></li><li><p><strong>Hex Synergy.</strong> In <em>Any hex your faction has held for 3+ Strategic Turns</em> hexes, your faction gains +1 on defense checks in that hex.</p></li><li><p><strong>Second-Form Bearing.</strong> Once per Strategic Turn, your faction may treat one Morale or Loyalty check as if it had one additional track-band of headroom. The thing you became has held under pressure before.</p></li></ul><div data-ft-per-use=\"1\" style=\"margin-top:0.7rem;padding:0.55rem 0.75rem;border:1px solid #6a8caa;border-radius:0.35rem;background:rgba(55,75,95,0.18);\"><p><span style=\"letter-spacing: 0.04em; text-transform: uppercase; color: #a8c4e0; margin-bottom: 0.25rem; font-size: 0.78rem\">⟁ Per-Use Ability — <strong>Hex Recognition</strong></span> <span style=\"opacity: 0.92; line-height: 1.4; font-size: 0.86rem\"><strong>Recovery:</strong> 1/scene  ·  <strong>Action:</strong> Action  ·  <strong>Use:</strong> Click this feature on your sheet to invoke.</span> <span style=\"opacity: 0.85; margin-top: 0.3rem; font-size: 0.82rem\">On a natural surface you're touching, whisper a question — GM answers with one true thing the land knows.</span></p></div>",
      "chat": ""
    },
